  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The general displacement of a simple harmonic oscillator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> be its time period. The slope of its potential energy (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi></math>) &ndash; time (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>) curve will be maximum when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here, displacement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, potential energy of a simple harmonic oscillator is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So, slope of potential energy and time curve is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;will be maximum when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>"
  }
}